{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ca9872365d19649d","x":-700,"y":-340,"width":1320,"height":620,"type":"text","text":"Born in Yormindar, Saggnus Wildbottom, is a dwarven man whose family has a unknown connection the Archdevil of Avernus, Zahriel. At a young age my father was working the mines, while my mother raised me at home. We were not of noble status and for the most part had a fairly average life. I began to show interest in my father's work at around age 30 and so, often he would take me into the residuum mines on his working days. At age 40 my father became erratic, speaking of different realms and whole new ways of life that seemed dark and twisted. By age 50, I was no longer close with my father, I got a job working the mines and began thinking of my own future. So I worked for 150 years, just turning 200 years old I got a promotion and a raise, I became the foreman of the Hall of Glowing Mushrooms. \n\nOne day while working different locations, my father didn't come back from the job. We sent search parties, rescue team, and many more, but could not find any evidence of anything. We assumed he was dead. I couldn't accept it, a death without the full story, I needed to know what happened. Well searching through his things, I found a ring, forged with obsidian and molten lava flowing through the center of the ring. As I lifted the ring, I felt compelled to wear it, and as I placed it on my finger and twisted my hand it formed into a dark obsidian spear with burning flames at the head of the spear. As the magical spear appeared in my hand I heard a voice in my head and my vision went dark. As I opened my eyes I was on a battlefield. Corpses lined an ashen wasteland, blood everywhere, in the sky a gigantic burning hand and as it approached closer and closer to me I began to see her, who I now know to be the Archdevil Zahriel. Sitting in the palm of this blazing hand clutching a chain that led to a shackle, a collar on the neck of the father I thought dead. The next words will resonate within me for the rest of my life, \"Become my slave, do as I see fit to the world I cannot come to. Bring me the daughters of the Lumiere, and your father may live. Refuse and you will be reunited once more,\" as another chain drops from the other hand and wrapped around my neck. I saw before me my cry father unable to speak in eternal suffering and a piece of paper blazing in fire to be signed in blood there was no other option. I have to save him, I sign the contract, but that wasn't the end, for 67 years she forced me to watch as she killed my father and resurrected him time and time again. Until she said \"It seems your quarry has awakened, I shall join on the surface shortly. Remember the past 6 decades, betray me and shall suffer a fate worse than that.\" And so I awakened back in my home my mother sitting on a chair looking at me as I awaken, tears in her eyes, I have been unconscious that entire time. I knew in my head to seek out the party members of Umbra VI and find them. I need to talk to Balgus my cousin. Given a direction and quest I marched forward as I made my way to the city of Volstar, I heard her voice again saying she would send a distraction to get me into the city. My job is to become friends with Umbra VI, help them, deceive them, and in the end when they are met face to face with my master, turn over Aralia Lumiere.\n\nI don't want to do it, but if I don't me and my father will be condemned to eternal damnation. When I woke up I gained new found powers with combat that I never had before. I also was given memories, visions of the kind of people Umbra VI are, who they helped, the suffering they have been through, and the goal the seek to achieve. Part of me wants to get their help, but what will become of me if I betray the Archdevil. That fear shackles me. I hope that they prove themselves capable of helping me even though I have nothing to give in return. And if they do not, I shall do her biding."},
		{"id":"dda1622cb02da5ba","x":-700,"y":-480,"width":250,"height":120,"type":"text","text":"Birth: \nPlace - Yormindar\nDate - 1,733 PD\nAge: 267"},
